WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:16.572
For the next three months, Mowgli didn’t leave the village.

2
00:00:16.573 --> 00:00:22.984
He was too busy learning the ways and customs of humans.

3
00:00:22.985 --> 00:00:27.076
First he found out he had to wear clothing all the time.

4
00:00:27.077 --> 00:00:30.615
"This is so annoying," he thought.

5
00:00:30.616 --> 00:00:33.756
His shirt felt itchy.

6
00:00:33.757 --> 00:00:37.854
His shoes pinched his toes.

7
00:00:37.855 --> 00:00:43.583
Then he had to learn how to count money, which he didn't understand at all.

8
00:00:43.584 --> 00:00:48.780
"Why do humans have to buy things from each other?" he asked Messua.

9
00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.377
"In the jungle you can just take what you want."

10
00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:58.431
Messua laughed. "That's a good question," she said.

11
00:00:58.432 --> 00:01:03.061
"I don't have an answer for you."

12
00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:08.081
On top of these things, the village children often made him angry.

13
00:01:08.082 --> 00:01:14.146
When they played games together, Mowgli stood by himself and watched.

14
00:01:14.147 --> 00:01:18.164
The girl laughed at him.

15
00:01:18.165 --> 00:01:22.390
"The jungle boy doesn't know how to play any games!"

16
00:01:22.391 --> 00:01:26.651
"He can't make a fire either," one of the boys added.

17
00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:30.923
"And he says the wrong words all the time."

18
00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:34.909
Mowgli felt angry but he stayed quiet.

19
00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.899
Whenever he got mad, he tried to think of Baloo.

20
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:45.099
"The law of the jungle says, keep your temper," the old bear had taught him.

21
00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:50.494
"In the jungle your life and food depend on this."

22
00:01:50.495 --> 00:02:02.880
Here in the village his life might depend on it too.

23
00:02:02.881 --> 00:02:09.228
One night Mowgli joined the circle that formed every evening under a fig tree.

24
00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:13.356
The people met to tell stories and gossip.

25
00:02:13.357 --> 00:02:16.933
Monkeys sat in the fig tree's upper branches.

26
00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.962
They chattered away for hours too.

27
00:02:19.963 --> 00:02:27.053
Mowgli listened as the people told tales about gods, humans, and ghosts.

28
00:02:27.054 --> 00:02:30.386
Buldeo was the village's chief hunter.

29
00:02:30.387 --> 00:02:35.005
He told long stories about all the beasts in the jungle.

30
00:02:35.006 --> 00:02:44.396
The children's eyes went wide as they listened to tales about panthers, elephants, and wild pigs.

31
00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.272
Mowgli had to cover his face.

32
00:02:47.273 --> 00:02:52.355
He didn't want anyone to see him laughing at Buldeo's silly tales.

33
00:02:52.356 --> 00:02:58.497
But as Buldeo told one story after another, Mowgli couldn't help himself.

34
00:02:58.498 --> 00:03:01.920
The boy's shoulders shook with laughter.

35
00:03:01.921 --> 00:03:06.149
Then Buldeo started a new ghost story.

36
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:10.870
"This ghost lives inside a jungle tiger's body.

37
00:03:10.871 --> 00:03:14.649
It's the tiger who stole Messua's son."

38
00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:17.527
"What?" Mowgli burst out.

39
00:03:17.528 --> 00:03:21.553
He couldn't sit there and stay quiet any longer.

40
00:03:21.554 --> 00:03:24.117
"The jungle tiger isn't a ghost.

41
00:03:24.118 --> 00:03:29.052
He's real. His name is Shere Khan."

42
00:03:29.053 --> 00:03:31.970
Everyone turned to stare at Mowgli.

43
00:03:31.971 --> 00:03:36.452
Buldeo was speechless with surprise for a few moments.

44
00:03:36.453 --> 00:03:38.832
Then he glared at the boy.

45
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:43.129
"Oh! The jungle brat is speaking up!

46
00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:47.662
If you're so wise, why don't you hunt down the tiger?

47
00:03:47.663 --> 00:03:51.867
There is a reward for his hide."

48
00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:57.025
"I will hunt him down one day," Mowgli said under his breath.

49
00:03:57.026 --> 00:04:05.837
The hunter sneered. "Well, from now on, keep your mouth shut when your elders are speaking."

50
00:04:05.838 --> 00:04:11.725
A few minutes later, Mowgli got up.

51
00:04:11.726 --> 00:04:16.565
"I've been listening all evening," he said loudly.

52
00:04:16.566 --> 00:04:22.800
"And Buldeo has spoken only one or two words of truth."

53
00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:27.654
As Mowgli left the circle, Buldeo puffed and snorted.

54
00:04:27.655 --> 00:04:32.282
"How dare the boy embarrass me like that!" the hunter said.

55
00:04:32.283 --> 00:04:37.331
"This is not something that I will forget."

56
00:04:37.332 --> 00:04:42.318
That night the priest visited Messua and her husband.

57
00:04:42.319 --> 00:04:47.160
He said it was time to give Mowgli a job.

58
00:04:47.161 --> 00:04:52.611
The next morning Mowgli was sent out with the other village children.

59
00:04:52.612 --> 00:05:00.601
From now on, he would help to herd the village's buffalo and cattle.
